IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 1: s 2 Interpretation -- the rest of the definitions, in the Act's alphabetical order.
-- (The definitions the TV question uses are in sgta-s2-definitions.l4.)
-- A definition that "includes" answers TRUE for the cases it lists and NOTHING for the rest: the Act does not say the list is exhaustive,
-- so a case it does not list is not thereby excluded.  A definition that "means" answers TRUE or FALSE.
-- A term the Act defines by pointing at another statute (premises, common property, VCC, Town Council, ...) takes that statute's meaning
-- as an input: the question whether a thing meets that other statute's definition is not this Act's to answer.

§ `s 2 Interpretation: opening words, Chief Executive, code of practice, common property`

-- src:268 | 2. In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 2 opening words (src:268-268)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: the definitions in s 2 apply to the term as used in this Act` MEANS
    (NOT `the context otherwise requires`)

-- src:278 | “Chief Executive”, in relation to the Authority, means the Chief
-- src:279 | Executive of the Authority appointed under section 40(2) of
-- src:280 | the Info‑communications Media Development Authority
-- src:281 | Act 2016, and includes any individual acting in that capacity;
@ref s 2 "Chief Executive" (src:278-281)
GIVEN `the person is the Chief Executive of the Authority appointed under section 40(2) of the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an individual acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this person is the "Chief Executive" in relation to the Authority` MEANS
    `the person is the Chief Executive of the Authority appointed under section 40(2) of the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016` OR `the person is an individual acting in that capacity`

-- src:283 | “code of practice” means a code of practice issued or approved
-- src:284 | under section 23 or 30;
@ref s 2 "code of practice" (src:283-284)
GIVEN `the code is issued or approved under section 23` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the code is issued or approved under section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a "code of practice"` MEANS
    `the code is issued or approved under section 23` OR `the code is issued or approved under section 30`

-- src:286 | “common property” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the
-- src:287 | Building (Strata Management) Act 2004;
-- src:289 | [Act 12 of 2020 wef 01/10/2025]
@ref s 2 "common property" (src:286-289)
GIVEN `it has the meaning section 2(1) of the Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 gives common property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is "common property"` MEANS
    `it has the meaning section 2(1) of the Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 gives common property`

§ `s 2 Interpretation: earthworks, Housing and Development Board, installation or plant`

-- src:291 | “earthworks” includes —
-- src:293 | (a) any act of excavating earth, rock or other material (by
-- src:294 | whatever means) in connection with —
-- src:296 | (i) any works for or relating to the construction,
-- src:297 | reconstruction, extension, renovation,
-- src:298 | alteration, demolition or repair of any
-- src:299 | building, road, railway, bridge, viaduct,
-- src:300 | flyover, sewer or sewage works;
-- src:302 | (ii) any works for or relating to the laying,
-- src:303 | inspecting, repairing or renewing of any
-- src:305 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:306 | 7 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:308 | mains, pipes, cables, fittings or other
-- src:309 | apparatuses;
-- src:311 | (iii) any soil investigation works; or
-- src:313 | (iv) such other works as are usually undertaken by a
-- src:314 | person carrying on business as a contractor in
-- src:315 | the construction industry or as a professional
-- src:316 | civil or structural engineer;
-- src:318 | (b) any act of boring, dredging, jacking, levelling, piling
-- src:319 | or tunnelling on or under any premises or street by
-- src:320 | any mechanical means; and
-- src:322 | (c) the driving or sinking of any earth rod, casing or tube
-- src:323 | into the ground;
@ref s 2 "earthworks" (src:291-323)
GIVEN `the act is excavating earth, rock or other material, by whatever means, in connection with works for or relating to the construction, reconstruction, extension, renovation, alteration, demolition or repair of a building, road, railway, bridge, viaduct, flyover, sewer or sewage works` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is excavating earth, rock or other material, by whatever means, in connection with works for or relating to the laying, inspecting, repairing or renewing of mains, pipes, cables, fittings or other apparatuses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is excavating earth, rock or other material, by whatever means, in connection with soil investigation works` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is excavating earth, rock or other material, by whatever means, in connection with such other works as are usually undertaken by a contractor in the construction industry or a professional civil or structural engineer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is boring, dredging, jacking, levelling, piling or tunnelling on or under any premises or street by any mechanical means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the driving or sinking of an earth rod, casing or tube into the ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2: this act is within "earthworks"` MEANS
    BRANCH IF    `the act is excavating earth, rock or other material, by whatever means, in connection with works for or relating to the construction, reconstruction, extension, renovation, alteration, demolition or repair of a building, road, railway, bridge, viaduct, flyover, sewer or sewage works`
              OR `the act is excavating earth, rock or other material, by whatever means, in connection with works for or relating to the laying, inspecting, repairing or renewing of mains, pipes, cables, fittings or other apparatuses`
              OR `the act is excavating earth, rock or other material, by whatever means, in connection with soil investigation works`
              OR `the act is excavating earth, rock or other material, by whatever means, in connection with such other works as are usually undertaken by a contractor in the construction industry or a professional civil or structural engineer`
              OR `the act is boring, dredging, jacking, levelling, piling or tunnelling on or under any premises or street by any mechanical means`
              OR `the act is the driving or sinking of an earth rod, casing or tube into the ground`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:335 | “Housing and Development Board” means the Housing and
-- src:336 | Development Board established by section 3 of the Housing
-- src:337 | and Development Act 1959;
@ref s 2 "Housing and Development Board" (src:335-337)
GIVEN `it is the Housing and Development Board established by section 3 of the Housing and Development Act 1959` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this body is the "Housing and Development Board"` MEANS
    `it is the Housing and Development Board established by section 3 of the Housing and Development Act 1959`

-- src:339 | “installation or plant used for telecommunications” includes all
-- src:340 | buildings, lands, structures, machinery, equipment, cables,
-- src:341 | poles and lines used or intended for use in connection with
-- src:342 | telecommunications;
@ref s 2 "installation or plant used for telecommunications" (src:339-342)
GIVEN `it is a building, land, structure, machinery, equipment, cable, pole or line` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used or intended for use in connection with telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is "installation or plant used for telecommunications"` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is a building, land, structure, machinery, equipment, cable, pole or line` AND `it is used or intended for use in connection with telecommunications`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2 Interpretation: owner`

-- src:348 | “owner” —
-- src:350 | (a) in relation to any premises comprised in a strata title
-- src:351 | plan under the Land Titles (Strata) Act 1967,
-- src:352 | means —
-- src:354 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:355 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 8
-- src:357 | (i) in the case of a lot, the person who is registered
-- src:358 | as the subsidiary proprietor of the lot under that
-- src:359 | Act;
-- src:361 | (ii) in the case of a common property, the
-- src:362 | management corporation having control of
-- src:363 | that common property, or the person
-- src:364 | receiving any rent or charge for the
-- src:365 | maintenance and management of that
-- src:366 | common property; and
-- src:368 | (iii) in the case of a limited common property as
-- src:369 | defined in section 2(1) of the Building (Strata
-- src:370 | Management) Act 2004, the subsidiary
-- src:371 | management corporation established by the
-- src:372 | Building (Strata Management) Act 2004
-- src:373 | having control of that limited common
-- src:374 | property, or the person receiving any rent or
-- src:375 | charge for the maintenance and management of
-- src:376 | that limited common property;
-- src:378 | [Act 12 of 2020 wef 01/10/2025]
-- src:380 | (b) in relation to a building in a housing estate of the
-- src:381 | Housing and Development Board (called a HDB
-- src:382 | housing estate), means —
-- src:384 | (i) in the case of a flat, any owner of the flat as
-- src:385 | defined in section 2(1) of the Housing and
-- src:386 | Development Act 1959;
-- src:388 | (ii) in the case of the building’s common property
-- src:389 | in a HDB housing estate that is controlled,
-- src:390 | managed and maintained by a Town Council,
-- src:391 | that Town Council; and
-- src:393 | (iii) in the case of the building’s common property
-- src:394 | in a HDB housing estate that is not controlled,
-- src:395 | managed and maintained by a Town Council,
-- src:396 | the Housing and Development Board;
-- src:398 | (c) in relation to a subdivided building other than a
-- src:399 | subdivided building mentioned in paragraph (a) or
-- src:400 | (b), means —
-- src:402 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:403 | 9 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:405 | (i) in the case of a lot, the person who is registered
-- src:406 | under the Land Titles Act 1993 as the
-- src:407 | proprietor of the fee simple, estate in
-- src:408 | perpetuity or leasehold estate of that lot; and
-- src:410 | (ii) in the case of the subdivided building’s
-- src:411 | common property, every person who is
-- src:412 | registered under the Land Titles Act 1993 as
-- src:413 | the proprietor of the fee simple, estate in
-- src:414 | perpetuity or leasehold estate of a lot in that
-- src:415 | building, or the person receiving any rent or
-- src:416 | charge for the maintenance and management of
-- src:417 | the common property;
-- src:419 | (d) in relation to any premises which are not subdivided,
-- src:420 | means any person who is registered under the Land
-- src:421 | Titles Act 1993 as the proprietor of the fee simple,
-- src:422 | estate in perpetuity or leasehold estate of those
-- src:423 | premises; and
-- src:425 | (e) in relation to any other premises or building, means
-- src:426 | the person for the time being receiving the rent of the
-- src:427 | premises or building, whether on the person’s own
-- src:428 | account or as agent, trustee or receiver, or who would
-- src:429 | receive such rent if the premises or building were let
-- src:430 | to a tenant, and includes the person whose name is
-- src:431 | entered in the Valuation List prepared under
-- src:432 | section 10 of the Property Tax Act 1960 as the
-- src:433 | owner of the premises or building, or a mortgagee in
-- src:434 | possession;
@ref s 2 "owner" (src:348-434)
GIVEN `the person is registered as the subsidiary proprietor of the lot under the Land Titles (Strata) Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 "owner" (a)(i): the person is the owner of a lot in a strata title plan` MEANS
    `the person is registered as the subsidiary proprietor of the lot under the Land Titles (Strata) Act 1967`

GIVEN `the person is the management corporation having control of the common property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receives rent or a charge for the maintenance and management of the common property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 "owner" (a)(ii): the person is the owner of common property in a strata title plan` MEANS
    `the person is the management corporation having control of the common property` OR `the person receives rent or a charge for the maintenance and management of the common property`

GIVEN `the person is the subsidiary management corporation established by the Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 having control of the limited common property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receives rent or a charge for the maintenance and management of the limited common property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 "owner" (a)(iii): the person is the owner of limited common property in a strata title plan` MEANS
    `the person is the subsidiary management corporation established by the Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 having control of the limited common property` OR `the person receives rent or a charge for the maintenance and management of the limited common property`

GIVEN `the person is an owner of the flat as defined in section 2(1) of the Housing and Development Act 1959` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 "owner" (b)(i): the person is the owner of a flat in an HDB housing estate` MEANS
    `the person is an owner of the flat as defined in section 2(1) of the Housing and Development Act 1959`

GIVEN `the common property is controlled, managed and maintained by a Town Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is that Town Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Housing and Development Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 "owner" (b)(ii) and (iii): the person is the owner of the common property of a building in an HDB housing estate` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the common property is controlled, managed and maintained by a Town Council` THEN `the person is that Town Council`
           OTHERWISE `the person is the Housing and Development Board`

GIVEN `the person is registered under the Land Titles Act 1993 as the proprietor of the fee simple, estate in perpetuity or leasehold estate of the lot` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 "owner" (c)(i): the person is the owner of a lot in a subdivided building not within (a) or (b)` MEANS
    `the person is registered under the Land Titles Act 1993 as the proprietor of the fee simple, estate in perpetuity or leasehold estate of the lot`

GIVEN `the person is registered under the Land Titles Act 1993 as the proprietor of the fee simple, estate in perpetuity or leasehold estate of a lot in the building` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receives rent or a charge for the maintenance and management of the common property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 "owner" (c)(ii): the person is the owner of the common property of a subdivided building not within (a) or (b)` MEANS
    `the person is registered under the Land Titles Act 1993 as the proprietor of the fee simple, estate in perpetuity or leasehold estate of a lot in the building` OR `the person receives rent or a charge for the maintenance and management of the common property`

GIVEN `the person is registered under the Land Titles Act 1993 as the proprietor of the fee simple, estate in perpetuity or leasehold estate of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 "owner" (d): the person is the owner of premises that are not subdivided` MEANS
    `the person is registered under the Land Titles Act 1993 as the proprietor of the fee simple, estate in perpetuity or leasehold estate of the premises`

GIVEN `the person for the time being receives the rent of the premises or building, on own account or as agent, trustee or receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would receive the rent if the premises or building were let to a tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's name is entered in the Valuation List prepared under section 10 of the Property Tax Act 1960 as the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a mortgagee in possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 "owner" (e): the person is the owner of any other premises or building` MEANS
    `the person for the time being receives the rent of the premises or building, on own account or as agent, trustee or receiver`
    OR `the person would receive the rent if the premises or building were let to a tenant`
    OR `the person's name is entered in the Valuation List prepared under section 10 of the Property Tax Act 1960 as the owner`
    OR `the person is a mortgagee in possession`

§ `s 2 Interpretation: premises, public telecommunication licensee's installation or plant, securities, shares`

-- src:436 | “premises” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the
-- src:437 | Building Control Act 1989;
@ref s 2 "premises" (src:436-437)
GIVEN `it has the meaning section 2(1) of the Building Control Act 1989 gives premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: these are "premises"` MEANS
    `it has the meaning section 2(1) of the Building Control Act 1989 gives premises`

-- src:442 | “public telecommunication licensee’s installation or plant”
-- src:443 | means any installation or plant used for
-- src:444 | telecommunications belonging to or used by a public
-- src:445 | telecommunication licensee;
@ref s 2 "public telecommunication licensee's installation or plant" (src:442-445)
GIVEN `it is installation or plant used for telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it belongs to a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used by a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a "public telecommunication licensee's installation or plant"` MEANS
    `it is installation or plant used for telecommunications` AND (`it belongs to a public telecommunication licensee` OR `it is used by a public telecommunication licensee`)

-- src:464 | “securities”, in relation to a company (including a VCC),
-- src:465 | includes shares, debentures, bonds and other securities of the
-- src:466 | company, whether or not constituting a charge on the assets
-- src:467 | of the company;
-- src:469 | [S 26/2022 wef 13/01/2022]
@ref s 2 "securities" (src:464-469)
GIVEN `it is a share, debenture, bond or other security of the company, whether or not it constitutes a charge on the assets of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is "securities" in relation to a company (including a VCC)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is a share, debenture, bond or other security of the company, whether or not it constitutes a charge on the assets of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:471 | “shares” includes stock;
@ref s 2 "shares" (src:471-471)
GIVEN `it is stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a "share"` MEANS
    `it is a share` OR `it is stock`

§ `s 2 Interpretation: standard of performance, street, telecommunication cable and cable detection`

-- src:473 | “standard of performance” means a standard of performance
-- src:474 | issued or approved under section 30;
@ref s 2 "standard of performance" (src:473-474)
GIVEN `the standard is issued or approved under section 30` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a "standard of performance"` MEANS
    `the standard is issued or approved under section 30`

-- src:476 | “street” includes any way, road, lane, path, passage or open
-- src:477 | space, whether a thoroughfare or not, over which the public
-- src:478 | have a right of way and also the roadway and footway over
-- src:479 | any public bridge and includes any road, footway or passage,
-- src:480 | used or intended to be used as a means of access to 2 or more
-- src:481 | holdings, whether the public has a right of way thereover or
-- src:482 | not;
@ref s 2 "street" (src:476-482)
GIVEN `it is a way, road, lane, path, passage or open space over which the public have a right of way, whether a thoroughfare or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the roadway or footway over a public bridge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a road, footway or passage used or intended to be used as a means of access to 2 or more holdings, whether or not the public has a right of way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a "street"` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it is a way, road, lane, path, passage or open space over which the public have a right of way, whether a thoroughfare or not` OR `it is the roadway or footway over a public bridge` OR `it is a road, footway or passage used or intended to be used as a means of access to 2 or more holdings, whether or not the public has a right of way`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:487 | “telecommunication cable” means any cable of a
-- src:488 | telecommunication system belonging to or under the
-- src:489 | management or control of a telecommunication system
-- src:490 | licensee;
@ref s 2 "telecommunication cable" (src:487-490)
GIVEN `it is a cable of a telecommunication system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system belongs to or is under the management or control of a telecommunication system licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a "telecommunication cable"` MEANS
    `it is a cable of a telecommunication system` AND `the system belongs to or is under the management or control of a telecommunication system licensee`

-- src:492 | “telecommunication cable detection work” means any work of
-- src:493 | detecting or locating any underground telecommunication
-- src:494 | cable;
@ref s 2 "telecommunication cable detection work" (src:492-494)
GIVEN `the work is detecting or locating an underground telecommunication cable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is "telecommunication cable detection work"` MEANS
    `the work is detecting or locating an underground telecommunication cable`

-- src:499 | “telecommunication cable detection worker” means any person
-- src:500 | whose trade or occupation requires or includes the personal
-- src:501 | performance by him or her of telecommunication cable
-- src:502 | detection work;
@ref s 2 "telecommunication cable detection worker" (src:499-502)
GIVEN `the person's trade or occupation requires or includes the personal performance by the person of telecommunication cable detection work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this person is a "telecommunication cable detection worker"` MEANS
    `the person's trade or occupation requires or includes the personal performance by the person of telecommunication cable detection work`

-- src:504 | “telecommunication cable detection work licence” means a
-- src:505 | licence granted under section 34;
@ref s 2 "telecommunication cable detection work licence" (src:504-505)
GIVEN `the licence is granted under section 34` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a "telecommunication cable detection work licence"` MEANS
    `the licence is granted under section 34`

§ `s 2 Interpretation: telecommunication line, Town Council, VCC`

-- src:510 | “telecommunication line” means a wire or cable used for
-- src:511 | telecommunications with any casing, coating, tube or pipe
-- src:512 | enclosing the same and any appliance and apparatus
-- src:513 | connected therewith for the purpose of fixing or insulating
-- src:514 | the same;
@ref s 2 "telecommunication line" (src:510-514)
GIVEN `it is a wire or cable used for telecommunications, with any casing, coating, tube or pipe enclosing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an appliance or apparatus connected with such a wire or cable for the purpose of fixing or insulating it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a "telecommunication line"` MEANS
    `it is a wire or cable used for telecommunications, with any casing, coating, tube or pipe enclosing it` OR `it is an appliance or apparatus connected with such a wire or cable for the purpose of fixing or insulating it`

-- src:538 | “Town Council” means a Town Council established by section 4
-- src:539 | of the Town Councils Act 1988;
@ref s 2 "Town Council" (src:538-539)
GIVEN `it is a Town Council established by section 4 of the Town Councils Act 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this body is a "Town Council"` MEANS
    `it is a Town Council established by section 4 of the Town Councils Act 1988`

-- src:544 | “VCC” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the VCC Act;
@ref s 2 "VCC" (src:544-544)
GIVEN `it has the meaning section 2(1) of the VCC Act gives VCC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is a "VCC"` MEANS
    `it has the meaning section 2(1) of the VCC Act gives VCC`

-- src:548 | “VCC Act” means the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018;
@ref s 2 "VCC Act" (src:548-548)
GIVEN `it is the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2: this is the "VCC Act"` MEANS
    `it is the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018`
